 >>[2026-10-03 10:20] revise — Retracted the parser pathology. The 3634 s and 2728 s parse times match two macOS sleep intervals to within 20 seconds (pmset log: 14:09:24 to 15:10:16, 3652 s; 15:10:32 to 15:56:16, 2744 s, on battery at 0 percent); the timing script used wall-clock Date.now, which counts sleep. The snapshot of the file taken during the slow window parses in 880 ms. Lesson: time parses with process.cpuUsage or a monotonic clock and record wall time beside it; keep the machine awake (caffeinate) during waves.
